    "title": "Where is McNeese State located?",
    "text": "March 19, 2026, 2:45 p.m. ETMcNeese State is going through the best stretch in program history, winning 86 games the last three seasons with NCAA men's basketball tournament invitations to cap each one. The success of Will Wade -- one of the game's most controversial head coaches -- has carried on even after he left for North Carolina State last spring.That's thanks to the stewardship of Bill Armstrong, who made his first season as a Division I head coach an undeniable success. The former Wade assistant at LSU powered through all the roster attrition you'd expect from a coaching change in the NIL era and proved himself worthy of some Power 5 candidate buzz. Armed with a trio of former top-100 recruits (Garwey Dual, Jerrell Colbert and Larry Johnson), his Cowboys have the talent to upend a Vanderbilt Commodores team that was done few favors by the NCAA Selection Committee.Where will McNeese be making the trip to Oklahoma City from?McNeese State is located in Lake Charles, LouisianaLake Charles is a city that, unsurprisingly, sits on the bank of Lake Charles in the southwestern corner of the state. That leaves it roughly 210 miles from New Orleans and 145 from Houston.",
